Z||000000||merlin||01-27-2001||07:53 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/cwith15693/images/cat.jpg"> <BR>I recently bought this Catalytic Converter kit from the Fierostore for the V6 and I have some questions regarding the installation.  I should mention (a little venting here) that the kit was devoid of any type of instructions, which is why I have these questions.  Anyway my first issue is that the diameter of manifold pipe that is included with the kit and the pipes on the Cat are the same diameter.  One doesn’t fit into the other.  Do I need purchase an adapter for this, as the only hardware that’s included with the kit are muffler clamps.  In addition, I thought that the Cat had to be installed in one direction  and there is definitely no arrow or any indication on the converter as to what direction the flow is.  Thanks for any help.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||88formula||01-27-2001||09:34 PM||||I purchased that same kit from the Fiero Store and the pipe that I got did fit over the catalytic converter inlet pipe. You can use the catalytic converter any way you want; it's not directional. I would call the Fiero Store and tell them about your situation and tell them that mine fits over the converter. They have great service and will remedy your situation. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||TheFiero64||01-28-2001||11:09 AM||||I got the same kit. On mine the pipe also fit over the cat end.||||reg||1
